---
// Problem — Section 02 of the Wayfare case study
const reasons = [
  ['Separate tickets feel risky', 'If the two legs are on different airlines, the second won’t wait, and the first ticket won’t cover a missed connection.'],
  ['Trade-offs are hard to weigh', 'Time saved vs. money saved vs. layover length vs. self-transfer risk, four variables, and no tool that compares them side by side.'],
  ['“What if I miss the second flight?”', 'No safety net, no plan B, no one to call. The fear alone is enough to send people back to the simple, pricier direct flight.'],
];
---

<section class="wf-section problem">
  <div class="wf-wrap">
    <p class="wf-eyebrow">02 · Problem &amp; Background</p>
    <h2 class="wf-h2">The smartest route is one the big sites never show you.</h2>
    <p class="wf-intro">
      Every booking site shows the same thing, direct flights, or connections sold by a single airline. But the
      cheapest or fastest path is often one you have to assemble yourself: fly Delhi → Dubai on one ticket, then
      Dubai → Europe on another. Few travellers attempt it, because separate tickets feel risky and the trade-offs
      are hard to weigh.
    </p>

    <div class="compare">
      <article class="cmp cmp-neutral">
        <p class="cmp-label">What the big sites show</p>
        <h3 class="cmp-title">One airline, one ticket</h3>
        <div class="cmp-pill">
          <span class="code">DEL</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
          <span class="code">LHR</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cmp-body">Direct or single-airline connection. Simple to book, but frequently the most expensive or slowest option on the board.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="cmp cmp-blue">
        <p class="cmp-label">The path you'd assemble yourself</p>
        <h3 class="cmp-title">Two tickets, one smarter route</h3>
        <div class="cmp-pill">
          <span class="code">DEL</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
          <span class="code">DXB</span>
          <span class="plus">+</span>
          <span class="code">DXB</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
          <span class="code">LHR</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cmp-body">Two separate tickets on different airlines. Often cheaper or faster, but no big site assembles it, prices it, or tells you what happens if you miss the connection.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="why-head">Why few travellers attempt it</h3>
    <div class="reasons">
      {reasons.map(([title, body]) => (
        <article class="reason">
          <span class="reason-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h4 class="reason-title">{title}</h4>
          <p class="reason-body">{body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .compare {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  }
  .cmp {
    border: 1px solid var(--wf-border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--wf-surface-muted);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  }
  .cmp-blue {
    background: var(--wf-primary-tint);
    border-color: var(--wf-primary);
  }
  .cmp-label {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--wf-text-muted);
  }
  .cmp-blue .cmp-label { color: var(--wf-primary-text); }
  .cmp-title {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 1.2rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--wf-text);
  }
  .cmp-pill {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--wf-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--wf-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .cmp-pill .code {
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--wf-text);
  }
  .cmp-pill .arrow,
  .cmp-pill .plus {
    color: var(--wf-text-muted);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .cmp-blue .cmp-pill .code,
  .cmp-blue .cmp-pill .arrow,
  .cmp-blue .cmp-pill .plus {
    color: var(--wf-primary-text);
  }
  .cmp-body {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--wf-text-muted);
  }

  .why-head {
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.4vw, 1.9rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--wf-text);
  }
  .reasons {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  }
  .reason {
    border: 1px solid var(--wf-border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--wf-surface-muted);
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 2vw, 1.75rem);
  }
  .reason-tick {
    display: block;
    width: 32px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--wf-danger);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .reason-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--wf-text);
  }
  .reason-body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--wf-text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .reasons { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
